New fix, group R10-FLY-GH-READ-RETRY, PR 1 of 2, topic r10-fly-gh-read-retry. The full group spec and brief are on origin/handoff/audit-r10-roster (dev/programme/rosters/wave-r10-groups.json, group R10-FLY-GH-READ-RETRY, at 1ff0eb46 or later); read it first, and the assessor's P20 decision is quoted in it. Scope of THIS PR: tools/pr/app_approve.sh only (plus tools/audit/seat/INSTRUMENTS.md if the instrument description changes). Do not touch merge_train.py or record_row.py: that is PR 2, which waits on #2585, #2584 and #2524.
What to build: app_approve.sh's GitHub READS (the four gh api/gh pr view reads) retry with bounded backoff 5/15/45 s, reusing the existing pattern in tools/pr/app_push.sh (around l.188-251; prefer factoring a shared helper over copying, if that is architecturally sound). Retry ONLY on transport errors, HTTP 5xx, 429 and a secondary-rate-limit 403. Refuse immediately on 401, a permission 403, 404 or 422, or on a readable but wrong answer (head moved, verdict missing). Never retry writes (the review post).
Evidence: the cause was train 8 dying at 21:50:38Z on `app_approve: REFUSE: could not read pull request #2547` after a 2667 s CI wait. Pin it with a test that fails today.
Null controls, each a self-test case: (a) one transient failure then success makes exactly 2 calls and passes; (b) a 404 or wrong head makes exactly 1 call and refuses; (c) an exhausted budget refuses naming the last error. Mutation proof: removing the retry, retrying on 404, and retrying a write must each fail a check.
Follow dev/governance/roles/fixer.md: failing test first, mutation table, the finder's harness at both ends. PREPR_SKIP_CLOSURES=1. Body per .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md. ## Red checks: nightly-status grades main, and main's ci-ratchet red is runner-speed variance owned by R10-CI-LAYOUT. Apply standing rule 19 to every observation (Carry: <GROUP> | #<issue> | dismissed: <reason of 2+ words>, then (item <id>)), verified with python3 tools/audit/carry_audit.py --roster-ref origin/handoff/audit-r10-roster check --body <body.md>. Push code to handoff/r10-fly-gh-read-retry and the body with bash tools/audit/seat/body_push.sh r10-fly-gh-read-retry <body.md>; the handoff-body push is your return signal.
